+# Employee card scopes
+
+The global `TENANT_SCOPED_ACCESS_ENABLED` flag remains off by default. Employee matrix cells expose only implemented `view` and `update`. Self means the employee's own tenant membership; department compares current database department IDs within the same company. Null departments grant no department scope. An absent cell preserves the former `employees:manage` admission; explicit none denies that action.
+
+GET `/api/platform/members` and `/api/platform/me` member previews use the same filtered list. There is no employee pagination/count/options API in this version; all returned identity, role, contact, WhatsApp and editability fields belong only to rows selected by the scoped SQL. The list reads current membership/workflow while holding the shared tenant/policy/membership fences. Department moves use the existing exclusive tenant fence. Writes lock tenant, policies and actor/target memberships and re-evaluate independent update scope. Legacy upsert, deactivation and number mutation entry points use those same fences.
+
+The UI uses separate read/update flags and row-level `editable_fields`. Read-only users can open cards without receiving editable controls; creation, invitations and access-request tabs remain behind the coarse management flag. Access revocation clears cards and closes the editor. Existing owner/admin target protections and owner-only account-credential/profile assignment paths remain authoritative.
+
+Non-owner self update retains only the previously permitted WhatsApp recognition-number edits. Own role, status, display alias, permissions, department and access settings are not newly editable. The existing password-change route remains separate from employee administration.
+
+## Deliberately unresolved operations
+
+There is no employee deletion operation. Deactivation/reactivation is a membership update, not a fabricated delete grant. Creation/provisioning/invitations do exist but have no department-target input and a new employee is not the acting employee's own card. Therefore create is not yet advertised in the scoped catalog. A non-owner with an explicit employee scope cannot enter unconverted coarse creation/invitation flows; owner and wholly legacy flows are unchanged. To extend creation, specify how a new member's department is selected and whether scoped creators may assign it; do not infer `self` creation or change account credential rules. No further self-field decision is required to preserve today's safe update behavior.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `tests/test_employee_card_scopes.py`: four levels, independent read/update, two departments/tenants, sparse and gate-off behavior, protected self fields, SQL parameters and capabilities.
+- `tests/test_employee_card_scopes_postgres.py`: real filtered identity lists, department moves, revocation, write fences, denied self privilege edits and independent update with no read. Requires disposable localhost PostgreSQL.
+- `tests/test_employee_card_scopes_ui.cjs`: actual app read-only card, hidden management controls, revocation cleanup and zero writes.
